// name :
"P3735629181" "Building a Better Vermin"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeOneClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4122231206" "Building a Better Vermin"
// DetailString :
"P3328466434" "It all started when Terrence Dobbs asked you to help cull some of the Arachnoid population down in the Gutter of Grandville. Dobbs thanked you for your assistance, but commented on how he wish he had a better weapon for dealing with the Arachnoids."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ArachnoidX 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2529670636" "Crey Arachnoid-X76 Gas Canister"
// DetailString :
"P693377097" "The label on the gas canister says: 'Crey Arachnoid-X76 - For use against accelerated mutation type A-456 codenamed Arachnoid. HIGHLY TOXIC.' Apparently, Crey is quite versed in Arachnoid control already."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FieldTest 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2009785713" "Crey A-X76 Field Test Reports"
// DetailString :
"P2714622107" "These are field report tests on the effectiveness of the Crey A-X76 gas on the A-456 test subjects, citing a favorably deadly effect. The field report tests give coordinates to caves underneath St. Martial."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeTwoClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4094298167" "It all started when Terrence Dobbs asked you to help cull some of the Arachnoid population down in the Gutter of Grandville. Dobbs thanked you for your assistance, but commented on how he wish he had a better weapon for dealing with the Arachnoids.<br><br>Dobbs heard from one of his contacts that Crey was working on some bio-weapons at one of their labs in Cap Au Diable, and wanted you to break in and see if you could find anything to use against the Arachnoids. You found a weapon alright, along with indications that Crey was doing extensive research on the Arachnoids!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ArachnoidTag 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1782169923" "Arachnoid Tag"
// DetailString :
"P2875244637" "This small tag was found stapled onto the ear of the head Arachnoid. It says, 'A-456-053' along with the Crey Industries logo on it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeThreeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3570224994" "It all started when Terrence Dobbs asked you to help cull some of the Arachnoid population down in the Gutter of Grandville. Dobbs thanked you for your assistance, but commented on how he wish he had a better weapon for dealing with the Arachnoids.<br><br>Dobbs heard from one of his contacts that Crey was working on some bio-weapons at one of their labs in Cap Au Diable, and wanted you to break in and see if you could find anything to use against the Arachnoids. You found a weapon alright, along with indications that Crey was doing extensive research on the Arachnoids!<br><br>Dobbs wanted to find out more, and sent you to investigate some caves under St. Martial where Crey supposedly was conducting field tests. You found a number of Crey there in some Arachnoid tunnels, as well as a tagged Arachnoid marked as a research subject!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ResearchFiles 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P404342646" "Crey Research on A-456"
// DetailString :
"P1676044417" "These are a series of files on the test subjects known as A-456, otherwise known as Arachnoids. It looks like Crey has been doing research on the Arachnoids in an attempt to make a trained group of mutant shock troops while developing a series of countermeasures to any Arachnos-controlled Arachnoids. The project lead is a Crey scientist named Doctor Reaved based out of a Crey tech facility in Paragon City."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFourClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P840075759" "It all started when Terrence Dobbs asked you to help cull some of the Arachnoid population down in the Gutter of Grandville. Dobbs thanked you for your assistance, but commented on how he wish he had a better weapon for dealing with the Arachnoids.<br><br>Dobbs heard from one of his contacts that Crey was working on some bio-weapons at one of their labs in Cap Au Diable, and wanted you to break in and see if you could find anything to use against the Arachnoids. You found a weapon alright, along with indications that Crey was doing extensive research on the Arachnoids!<br><br>Dobbs wanted to find out more, and sent you to investigate some caves under St. Martial where Crey supposedly was conducting field tests. You found a number of Crey there in some Arachnoid tunnels, as well as a tagged Arachnoid marked as a research subject!<br><br>Dobbs sent you to check out the Crey office nearby the Arachnoid tunnels found on St. Martial. There, you found research files detailing how Crey was developing Arachnoid countermeasures to deal with any Arachnos-controlled threat, as well as developing a new strain of Arachnoids which Crey could use as shock troops!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFiveClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1351078601" "It all started when Terrence Dobbs asked you to help cull some of the Arachnoid population down in the Gutter of Grandville. Dobbs thanked you for your assistance, but commented on how he wish he had a better weapon for dealing with the Arachnoids.<br><br>Dobbs heard from one of his contacts that Crey was working on some bio-weapons at one of their labs in Cap Au Diable, and wanted you to break in and see if you could find anything to use against the Arachnoids. You found a weapon alright, along with indications that Crey was doing extensive research on the Arachnoids!<br><br>Dobbs wanted to find out more, and sent you to investigate some caves under St. Martial where Crey supposedly was conducting field tests. You found a number of Crey there in some Arachnoid tunnels, as well as a tagged Arachnoid marked as a research subject!<br><br>Dobbs sent you to check out the Crey office nearby the Arachnoid tunnels found on St. Martial. There, you found research files detailing how Crey was developing Arachnoid countermeasures to deal with any Arachnos-controlled threat, as well as developing a new strain of Arachnoids which Crey could use as shock troops!<br><br>Dobbs felt he was in over his head, and so decided to turn matters over to Arachnos. He got you take all the evidence to Arbiter Daos, who decided to enact protocols to shut down the Crey Arachnoid research operations."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL8_GV_Dobbs_Story_Arc_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3548601643" "Altered Arachnoid DNA"
// tDetailString :
"P594495968" "This is a sample of altered Arachnoid DNA that Crey Industries was fooling around with in a tale you like to call:<br><br><b>Building a Better Vermin</b><br><br>It all started when Terrence Dobbs asked you to help cull some of the Arachnoid population down in the Gutter of Grandville. Dobbs thanked you for your assistance, but commented on how he wish he had a better weapon for dealing with the Arachnoids.<br><br>Dobbs heard from one of his contacts that Crey was working on some bio-weapons at one of their labs in Cap Au Diable, and wanted you to break in and see if you could find anything to use against the Arachnoids. You found a weapon alright, along with indications that Crey was doing extensive research on the Arachnoids!<br><br>Dobbs wanted to find out more, and sent you to investigate some caves under St. Martial where Crey supposedly was conducting field tests. You found a number of Crey there in some Arachnoid tunnels, as well as a tagged Arachnoid marked as a research subject!<br><br>Dobbs sent you to check out the Crey office nearby the Arachnoid tunnels found on St. Martial. There, you found research files detailing how Crey was developing Arachnoid countermeasures to deal with any Arachnos-controlled threat, as well as developing a new strain of Arachnoids which Crey could use as shock troops!<br><br>Dobbs felt he was in over his head, and so decided to turn matters over to Arachnos. He got you take all the evidence to Arbiter Daos, who decided to enact protocols to shut down the Crey Arachnoid research operations.<br><br>Arbiter Daos sent you to the main Crey research facility in Paragon City to deal with the Crey scientist responsible for the Arachnoid reseach project and destroy their main database. Having dealt with the Crey threat to Arachnos security, Arbiter Daos gave you his thanks."

